  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so all design dimensions carry maximum uncertainty. The most informative first step is to establish the simplest possible performance baseline: RNA-only, single-profile, PCA (2000 components). This tells us (1) whether the task is tractable with minimal modeling, (2) what performance floor to compare against when adding complexity (better encoders, multiprofile aggregation, image modality, fusion), and (3) whether the RNA signal alone is sufficient or whether multimodal integration is necessary. Every subsequent experiment can be interpreted as a delta over this reference, making it the highest-information-per-experiment choice under a tight budget. It is also computationally inexpensive, reducing the risk of a costly failure on the first run."
